WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.958
(mechanism locking)

00:00:01.958 --> 00:00:05.050
(soft reminiscent piano music)

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:08.717
- There is no manual
on how to be a lampist.

00:00:10.492 --> 00:00:14.659
It takes many, many years to
learn all the facets of the job.

00:00:17.656 --> 00:00:19.943
At the peak of the
profession there were about

00:00:19.943 --> 00:00:21.943
800 lampists nationally.

00:00:23.748 --> 00:00:27.870
And I am, really, one of the
last people who are doing it.

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:31.787
(soft reminiscent piano music)

00:00:34.981 --> 00:00:38.648
My name is Jim Woodward,
and I am a lampist.

00:00:39.982 --> 00:00:41.315
That's what I do.

00:00:41.315 --> 00:00:44.084
(high-pitched bells chiming mystically)

00:00:44.084 --> 00:00:47.041
Well, a lampist is the specialist

00:00:47.041 --> 00:00:50.008
who works with lighthouse lenses.

00:00:50.008 --> 00:00:52.166
Maintenance of them, moving of them,

00:00:52.166 --> 00:00:54.597
disassembly, reassembly,

00:00:54.597 --> 00:00:57.768
just about everything there is to do.

00:00:57.768 --> 00:01:00.980
This one, I believe, is an impact break.

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:04.155
When I do an initial
inspection of the lens,

00:01:04.155 --> 00:01:08.443
I will go over every prism
and check every joint.

00:01:08.443 --> 00:01:10.702
You literally tap.

00:01:10.702 --> 00:01:13.017
And then I will do an audio check

00:01:13.017 --> 00:01:14.845
of every prism in the lens.

00:01:14.845 --> 00:01:17.095
You can almost play a tune.

00:01:19.157 --> 00:01:21.657
It requires infinite patience.

00:01:23.014 --> 00:01:24.231
Beautiful.

00:01:24.231 --> 00:01:25.481
Just beautiful.

00:01:26.892 --> 00:01:30.516
The lampist profession started about 1850.

00:01:30.516 --> 00:01:32.909
So indeed, the lampists'
work was very important

00:01:32.909 --> 00:01:35.309
because without the lenses being

00:01:35.309 --> 00:01:38.356
completely operational, they were useless.

00:01:38.356 --> 00:01:41.116
So the lampist kept the lenses working,

00:01:41.116 --> 00:01:44.690
and the lighthouse keeper
kept them lit every night.

00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:48.107
So, together, they kept the sailors safe.

00:01:51.803 --> 00:01:54.120
As technology was developed,

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:58.303
the classical Fresnel
lens started to decline,

00:01:58.303 --> 00:02:02.495
and it didn't require
the services of lampists.

00:02:02.495 --> 00:02:06.002
It would be a shame to
let the profession die

00:02:06.002 --> 00:02:08.076
because, in the process, eventually,

00:02:08.076 --> 00:02:10.659
the lenses themselves will die.

00:02:11.932 --> 00:02:14.329
Today, people drive
around the country looking

00:02:14.329 --> 00:02:17.786
at lighthouses and think nothing of it.

00:02:17.786 --> 00:02:20.913
I almost feel a mystical kind of feeling

00:02:20.913 --> 00:02:23.146
when I get near, near a lighthouse.

00:02:23.146 --> 00:02:24.728
I have a real connection to it,

00:02:24.728 --> 00:02:28.790
and I feel extremely
fortunate to have had a life,

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:31.880
52 years now, of working with lenses.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:36.047
To me, it’s just the most
amazing thing in the world.

